breach.segment:
// SQL Server engine marker: excludes MySQL / PostgreSQL replicas that share this metric
WHERE ss > 0 AND (lag_n > 0 OR lag_n_before > 0)
// Breach conditions (any of):
//  - inactive: the latest lag sample is negative (5+ samples in the signal window). Cloud SQL
//    documents a negative replica_lag as "replication is inactive".
//  - lagging: the replica stayed behind for the WHOLE signal window (minimum lag >= 120 s),
//    i.e. it is not catching up after bursts. Requires ~5 minutes of samples.
//    Lower for latency-sensitive reads; raise for cross-region replicas.
//  - lag not reported: replica_lag was reported earlier in the hour (5+ samples) but not in
//    the last 15 minutes, while the instance is still up (5+ up samples, all 1). Replication
//    has stalled, or the replica was promoted.
| EVAL inactive = lag_n >= 5 AND lag_last < 0,
       lagging = lag_n >= 5 AND lag_min >= 120,
       not_reporting = lag_n == 0 AND lag_n_before >= 5 AND up_n >= 5 AND up_min == 1
| WHERE inactive OR lagging OR not_reporting
| EVAL reason = CASE(inactive, "replication inactive (negative lag)", lagging, "replica lagging", "replica_lag not reported")
| KEEP database_id, reason, lag_min, lag_max, lag_last, lag_last_seen
| SORT database_id
| LIMIT 100
